 17592186045417] [17592186068033 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bc57df2e-a9e1-5597-8c96-67142bcba8ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068034 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd013c82-9f8e-5dc8-90a2-6df6eafbdb0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068035 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068035 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068035 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e56c10e-8e6c-5bd8-b662-a1f587ffaa32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068036 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068036 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068036 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f1dc5f5-88de-5a6d-bab2-82e21ffb09ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068037 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78bed3c5-f6cd-5f4c-9007-067d7f3405af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068555 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068555 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $\\log_3{9} = 2$ is equivalent to $b^2 = 9$. What is the value of $b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0cd0e716-e9da-51ca-9c75-adedad1bf12d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068555 #edb/ref 1074 "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n> $\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare\n\n$$\n\\log_3{9} = 2\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\log_{b}{a} = x\n$$\n\nwe get $a = 9$, $b = 3$, and $x = 2$.\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to $3^2 = 9$. Consequently, $b = 3$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068556 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068556 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $\\log_{6}{1} = 0$ is equivalent to $b^0 = 1$. What is the value of $b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068556 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9eafa03-bc10-5dfd-a212-a662d26974ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068556 #edb/ref 1074 "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n> $\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare\n\n$$\n\\log_{6}{1} = 0\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\log_{b}{a} = x\n$$\n\nwe get $a = 1$, $b = 6$, and $x = 0$.\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to $6^0 = 1$. Consequently, $b = 6$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068557 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068557 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $\\log_{16}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{b} = 4$. What is the value of $b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "446ff062-5a2d-5178-9660-60bafae375fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068557 #edb/ref 1074 "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n> $\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare\n\n$$\n\\log_{16}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\log_{b}{a} = x\n$$\n\nwe get $a = 4$, $b = 16$, and\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n16^{1/2} = 4\n$$\n\nwhich is also equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16} = 4\n$$\n\nConsequently, $b = 16$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068558 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068558 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $\\log_{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{8} \\right) = -3$ is equivalent to $b^{-3} = \\dfrac{1}{8}$. What is the value of $b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068558 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2613759b-9a0e-59b1-952b-1d2a8a08b4f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068558 #edb/ref 1074 "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n> $\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare\n\n$$\n\\log_{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{8} \\right) = -3\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\log_{b}{a} = x\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\na = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\n$b = 2$, and $x = -3$.\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2^{-3} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $b = 2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting Equations From Logarithmic Form to Exponential Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068869 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2d99805e-a17a-57ef-ae56-85f3060b066a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068870 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068870 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068870 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting Equations From Logarithmic Form to Exponential Form with Exponents of Zero or One" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068870 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068870 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2812181f-7ccc-5609-a399-1cf68591a903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting Equations From Logarithmic Form to Exponential Form Using Fractional Powers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068871 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aedb775e-d1c1-54dd-b66a-a9351dff1d97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting Equations From Logarithmic Form to Exponential Form Using Negative Powers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068872 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c754b280-89d0-5a8b-a1bc-a1be3d3ffce6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1045 "Converting From Logarithmic to Exponential Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068984 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "869ed6af-0b10-50ce-bcc8-797d11374764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069191 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186066342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069191 #edb/ref 1069 "q-252598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069191 #edb/ref 1071 "If the equation $\\log_{25} 5 = \\frac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{b} = 5$, then $b =$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e32f2a81-d301-5b15-8a48-dc736c374d85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069477 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186068032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069477 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66511" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069477 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $\\log_{5} 5 = 1$ is equivalent to $b^{1} = 5$. What is the value of $b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069477 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5aa8fd4-f7ec-5fc2-9e44-57ad3643264d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069829 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069829 #edb/ref 1061 455501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069829 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "077084c4-e969-5566-9b83-62efaa598eb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069829 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069830 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069830 #edb/ref 1061 455502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069830 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c26247c0-b345-560a-ab6b-b4538d6ca211" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069830 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069831 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069831 #edb/ref 1061 455506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069831 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "92247bc9-cac9-5943-8dc6-7bb5dc519a9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069831 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069832 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069832 #edb/ref 1061 455509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069832 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "add57a11-4cab-5aa1-9a2d-67f8aecf8784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069832 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069833 #edb/ref 1061 455513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069833 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d904622-8149-513a-ac33-2bee1a0ea315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069833 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069965 #edb/ref 1064 "So far, we have expressed an exponential equation in logarithm form. We can also go the other way, and express a logarithmic equation in exponential form.\n\nRemember, the base of the logarithm is always the base of the exponential expression.\nFor instance, if we know that\n\n$$\n\\log_{\\color{blue}{2}}(8) = {\\color{red}{3}}\n$$\n\nwe could write this using an exponent as\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{2}}^{\\color{red}{3}} = 8\n$$\n\nIn general, the logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n> $\\log_{\\color{blue}b}{a} = {\\color{red}x}$ is equivalent to $a = {\\color{blue}b}^{\\color{red}x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069965 #edb/ref 1065 2864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069965 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2c0b02d2-c424-5af8-967f-1b8a92acc6a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069965 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
